<title>JAPAN: Fanuc surges on buying by foreigners.</title>
<headline>Fanuc surges on buying by foreigners.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Fanuc Ltd surged in Wednesday morning trade on the Tokyo Stock Exchange on buying by foreign brokerages, brokers said.</p>
<p>Fanuc was up 180 yen at 3,910 yen at 0138 GMT.  </p>
<p>Brokers said the buying was prompted by a Merrill Lynch report saying the brokerage would raise its allocation ratio for the machinery tool sector, which benefits from the weaker yen.</p>
<p>The shares ranked sixth in the list of top percentage gainers on the first section of the Tokyo Stock Exchange.</p>
